/span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-nonirredundant-axiomatization — Effective Irredundant Axiomatization Can Fail over Arithmetic"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d4ae73c2fc9ccebd\" href=\"?note=d4ae73c2fc9ccebd\" title=\"67-df-irredundant-axiomatization\">67-df-irredundant-axiomatization</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1b2d614db2eb3b87\" href=\"?note=1b2d614db2eb3b87\" title=\"67-lem-irredundant-axiomatization-criterion\">67-lem-irredundant-axiomatization-criterion</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"3dfb8d24daf96156\" href=\"?note=3dfb8d24daf96156\" title=\"67-lem-hypersimple-interval-existence\">67-lem-hypersimple-interval-existence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4acca08be2551459\" href=\"?note=4acca08be2551459\" title=\"67-thm-numeration-independent-complement\">67-thm-numeration-independent-complement</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"9c200c8ec3685766\" href=\"?note=9c200c8ec3685766\" title=\"67-df-numeration\">67-df-numeration</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"fde932e35a45d307\" href=\"?note=fde932e35a45d307\" title=\"67-df-independent-formula\">67-df-independent-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"b59d5ff6e43660a9\" href=\"?note=b59d5ff6e43660a9\" title=\"67-df-recursively-enumerable-predicate\">67-df-recursively-enumerable-predicate</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"4"},{"key":"source_label","html":"Theorem 7; strengthening noted after proof of Theorem4.8"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"58,70"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"69,81"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"locally-revised-not-source-reverified"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"本次检查定义接口、依赖与陈述形式；未重新核验原书PDF，未作机器证明"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"false"},{"key":"inherited_verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"inherited_source_proof_status","html":"来源陈述和书中反证链已核对；继承Lemma4.6外部存在证明和Theorem3.3算术化限制"},{"key":"machine_verified","html":"false"},{"key":"revision_date","html":"2026-10-14"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\supseteq Q\">\\(T\\supseteq Q\\)</span> 是一致的固定原始递归算术公理呈示；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_1,\\Pi_1\">\\(\\Sigma_1,\\Pi_1\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IA}_T,\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T,\\mathrm{Ax}_T,\\mathrm{Irred}_T,\\mathrm{REAx}\">\\(\\mathrm{IA}_T,\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T,\\mathrm{Ax}_T,\\mathrm{Irred}_T,\\mathrm{REAx}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"d4ae73c2fc9ccebd\" href=\"?note=d4ae73c2fc9ccebd\" title=\"67-df-irredundant-axiomatization\">67-df-irredundant-axiomatization</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Num}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{Num}_T\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Indep}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{Indep}_T\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"9c200c8ec3685766\" href=\"?note=9c200c8ec3685766\" title=\"67-df-numeration\">67-df-numeration</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"fde932e35a45d307\" href=\"?note=fde932e35a45d307\" title=\"67-df-independent-formula\">67-df-independent-formula</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}^{\\le1}[x]\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}^{\\le1}[x]\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_\\eta\">\\(E_\\eta\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Z_{\\eta,H}\">\\(Z_{\\eta,H}\\)</span> 在下式构造；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\eta(\\bar k)\">\\(\\eta(\\bar k)\\)</span> 表示对指定变量 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span> 无捕获数词代入。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RE}_1\">\\(\\mathrm{RE}_1\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-13\" data-note=\"b59d5ff6e43660a9\" href=\"?note=b59d5ff6e43660a9\" title=\"67-df-recursively-enumerable-predicate\">67-df-recursively-enumerable-predicate</a>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}^{\\le1}[x]&amp;\\coloneqq\\{\\eta\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}:\\mathrm{free}_{L_A}(\\eta)\\subseteq\\{x\\}\\},\\\\\nE_\\eta&amp;\\coloneqq\\{\\eta(\\bar k):k\\in\\mathbb N\\},\\\\\nZ_{\\eta,H}&amp;\\coloneqq\\{\\eta(\\bar k):k\\in\\mathbb N\\setminus H\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}^{\\le1}[x]&amp;\\coloneqq\\{\\eta\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}:\\mathrm{free}_{L_A}(\\eta)\\subseteq\\{x\\}\\},\\\\\nE_\\eta&amp;\\coloneqq\\{\\eta(\\bar k):k\\in\\mathbb N\\},\\\\\nZ_{\\eta,H}&amp;\\coloneqq\\{\\eta(\\bar k):k\\in\\mathbb N\\setminus H\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall\\Gamma\\in\\{\\Pi_1,\\Sigma_1\\}\\ \\exists H\\subseteq\\mathbb N\\\n\\exists\\eta\\in\\Gamma\\cap\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}^{\\le1}[x]\\quad\n\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{RE}_1(H)\\land|\\mathbb N\\setminus H|=\\aleph_0\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Num}_T(\\eta,H)\\land\\mathrm{Indep}_T(\\eta,\\mathbb N\\setminus H)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\neg\\mathrm{IA}_T(T\\cup E_\\eta)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Ax}_T(Z_{\\eta,H},T\\cup E_\\eta)\n\\land\\mathrm{Irred}_T(Z_{\\eta,H})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\neg\\mathrm{REAx}(Z_{\\eta,H})\n\\land\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T(T\\cup E_\\eta).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall\\Gamma\\in\\{\\Pi_1,\\Sigma_1\\}\\ \\exists H\\subseteq\\mathbb N\\\n\\exists\\eta\\in\\Gamma\\cap\\mathrm{Fml}_{L_A}^{\\le1}[x]\\quad\n\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{RE}_1(H)\\land|\\mathbb N\\setminus H|=\\aleph_0\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Num}_T(\\eta,H)\\land\\mathrm{Indep}_T(\\eta,\\mathbb N\\setminus H)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\neg\\mathrm{IA}_T(T\\cup E_\\eta)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Ax}_T(Z_{\\eta,H},T\\cup E_\\eta)\n\\land\\mathrm{Irred}_T(Z_{\\eta,H})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\neg\\mathrm{REAx}(Z_{\\eta,H})\n\\land\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T(T\\cup E_\\eta).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>前半是原书 Theorem4.7，后半是印刷70页所作的明确对照。有效性限制是数学实质：这个反例有不可冗余的任意集合公理化，却没有不可冗余的r.e.公理化。</p>\n<p>取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-14\" data-note=\"3dfb8d24daf96156\" href=\"?note=3dfb8d24daf96156\" title=\"67-lem-hypersimple-interval-existence\">67-lem-hypersimple-interval-existence</a> 的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>，用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-15\" data-note=\"4acca08be2551459\" href=\"?note=4acca08be2551459\" title=\"67-thm-numeration-independent-complement\">67-thm-numeration-independent-complement</a> 取相应复杂度的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\eta\">\\(\\eta\\)</span>。成员实例已在 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> 中可证；非成员实例的有限正反指定一致，所以 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Z_{\\eta,H}\">\\(Z_{\\eta,H}\\)</span> 不可冗余且与全实例集相对演绎等价。补集无限还排除相对有限公理化。固定句法模板的数词实例集 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_\\eta\">\\(E_\\eta\\)</span> 是递归集：若无自由 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span>，它是单元素集；否则逐个核对固定模板及各替换位置的同一数词即可判定。因此可应用Lemma4.5的递归公理集前提。</p>\n<p>若假设 i.a.，Lemma4.5 给递归 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span>。令 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\chi_n=\\bigwedge_{k\\le n}\\eta(\\bar k)\">\\(\\chi_n=\\bigwedge_{k\\le n}\\eta(\\bar k)\\)</span>，有效搜索 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g(n)&gt;n\">\\(g(n)&gt;n\\)</span> 使 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+\\chi_{g(n)}\\vdash f(\\chi_n)\">\\(T+\\chi_{g(n)}\\vdash f(\\chi_n)\\)</span>。搜索会停，因为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+E_\\eta\\vdash f(\\chi_n)\">\\(T+E_\\eta\\vdash f(\\chi_n)\\)</span>；可增大有限支持的下标而确保 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g(n)&gt;n\">\\(g(n)&gt;n\\)</span>。由于 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\nvdash\\chi_n\\to f(\\chi_n)\">\\(T\\nvdash\\chi_n\\to f(\\chi_n)\\)</span>，必有 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\nvdash\\chi_n\\to\\chi_{g(n)}\">\\(T\\nvdash\\chi_n\\to\\chi_{g(n)}\\)</span>。递归定义 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h(0)=0\">\\(h(0)=0\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h(n+1)=g(h(n))\">\\(h(n+1)=g(h(n))\\)</span>。若某个 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(h(n),h(n+1)]\">\\((h(n),h(n+1)]\\)</span> 全在 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>，数值表示给 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> 证明全部新增实例，反而推出该被禁止的蕴涵，矛盾。Lemma4.6 保证存在这样的区间，从而排除 i.a.。</p>\n<p>最后，若 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Z_{\\eta,H}\">\\(Z_{\\eta,H}\\)</span> 是r.e.，它自身就是被排除的有效不可冗余公理化，所以它必非r.e.。这条推论无需假定 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\mapsto\\eta(\\bar k)\">\\(k\\mapsto\\eta(\\bar k)\\)</span> 在原句法上处处不同。全部反证依赖上述两条带限制的来源结果，因此本原子不升级为已核验证明依赖。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-irredundant-axiomatization","status":"resolved","id":"d4ae73c2fc9ccebd","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","exc